  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY NIGHT THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 211 PM MDT Fri Aug 21 2026\n\nMonsoon moisture will be present throughout most of the week. Sunday \nafternoon and evening has the strongest flooding signal for the \nAspen Acres burn scar with enough confidence for thunderstorm \ndevelopment further south across the region. The 500hPa high is \ncompressed enough in response to a wave passing to the north of the \nhigh to allow these storms to develop. So keep an eye out for a \nFlash Flood Watch for Sunday afternoon.  Monday through Wednesday \nhas a lot of similarities, however. The high is centered south of \nColorado and allows that monsoonal moisture over the west to advect \nover southern Colorado, so there will be daily chances for showers \nand thunderstorms over our mountains, mountain valleys, and plains. \nWe'll need to be on higher alert for flooding and flash flooding \nover urban areas, regions with saturated soils, and over our burn \nscars, including the Aspen Acres burn scar.",
